From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 22:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] dma: do not name ARM instructions in a portable
 resource

Same shape as 0013 did for usb2otg, and for the same reason. dma.resource is
otherwise portable -- its MMIO goes through AROS_LE2LONG/AROS_LONG2LE, its
peripheral base comes from KrnGetSystemAttr(KATTR_PeripheralBase), and its
completion IRQ goes through KrnAddIRQHandler() -- but two places spell a
barrier as inline AArch64:

    __asm__ __volatile__("dmb sy" ::: "memory");

which does not assemble for m68k, so the resource cannot be built for any
other CPU as written.

<asm/cpu.h> is where every ARM target already gets dmb(), and this target
supplies its own (added for the USB driver, 0013). Using it changes nothing on
ARM -- arch/arm-all's dmb() is that instruction -- and lets the resource build
here, where the honest answer is a compiler barrier: the guest is an m68k with
no barrier instruction to issue, what reaches the bus is AArch64 the JIT
emitted, and ordering against a device is Emu68's to guarantee. See the
comment in arch/m68k-emu68/include/asm/cpu.h.

Both sites are ordering a store to dma_Wait[].waiter against the IRQ handler
reading it, not ordering MMIO, so a compiler barrier is what the code actually
needs on this target.

Upstream would take this: naming the instruction was the accident, and every
ARM target keeps exactly the semantics it has today.

See AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0013.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/dma/dma_init.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/dma/dma_init.c b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/dma/dma_init.c
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/dma/dma_init.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/dma/dma_init.c
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@
 #include <proto/exec.h>
 #include <proto/dma.h>
 
+#include <asm/cpu.h>
+
 #include <hardware/bcm2708_dma.h>
 
 #include "dma_private.h"
@@ -255,7 +257,7 @@
         (dsig = AllocSignal(-1)) >= 0)
     {
         DMABase->dma_Wait[channel].sig = dsig;
-        __asm__ __volatile__("dmb sy" ::: "memory");
+        dmb();
         DMABase->dma_Wait[channel].waiter = FindTask(NULL);
 
         /* One reusable timer signal for the whole wait — the safety
@@ -321,7 +323,7 @@
         /* Stop the IRQ handler from signalling a bit we're about to free */
         Disable();
         DMABase->dma_Wait[channel].waiter = NULL;
-        __asm__ __volatile__("dmb sy" ::: "memory");
+        dmb();
         if (tsig >= 0)
             FreeSignal(tsig);
         FreeSignal(dsig);
